{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "18", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "17", "M": "20", "S": "33"}}, "news": [{"title": "BPTP targets \u20b93,000-5,000 crore annual sales, \u20b91,000 crore rental income in 5-7 years", "para": "BPTP is targeting annual sales of about \u20b93,000-5,000 crore while building a larger rental-yielding portfolio, Manik Malik, president and CEO, BPTP, told ETRealty. The company aims to increase annual rental income from around \u20b9100 crore currently to about \u20b91,000 crore over the next five to seven years.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/bptp-targets-3000-5000-crore-annual-sales-1000-crore-rental-income-in-5-7-years/134338974?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-30994/134338974.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Panchkula civic body launches extensive survey  in 42 villages to identify building violations", "para": "Panchkula municipal corporation has initiated a comprehensive survey across its 42 villages. Specialized teams are identifying structures built without necessary approvals or maps. Non-compliant property owners will receive notices to regularize or remove unauthorized constructions. The civic body aims for planned and systematic development within municipal limits. Enforcement efforts may face local political pressure despite recent sealing drives.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/panchkula-civic-body-launches-extensive-survey-in-42-villages-to-identify-building-violations/134338897?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-183968/134338897.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Double royalty row: Stone quarries, crushers, m-sand units across Karnataka to shut from September 18", "para": "Starting Friday